{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The phrase \"you, as successor-in-interest to DeNovo Music Group, Inc. and Steemer Corporation, respectively\" uses \"respectively\" with a single addressee, so which entity's rights Malmsteen personally took, and in what capacity, is not stated. The Agreement it amends names DeNovo Productions as \"Grantor,\" leaving unclear whether \"you\" in this letter is the Grantor bound by the operative paragraphs.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Only the first sentence of paragraph 1.02 was replaced, so the surviving option-exercise mechanics and the Minimum Recording Obligation schedule in paragraph 2.02 of the Agreement still contemplate three Option Periods only. Whether the fourth option carries the same exercise and Contract Period-end mechanics can only be answered by reading 1.02's unamended remainder with 2.02.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Paragraph 2.02's schedule of the Minimum Recording Obligation was never itself amended and lists no fourth Option Period, so this one-Album obligation exists only by the \"notwithstanding\" override. Whether the fourth Option Period's other incidents (Contract Period end under 1.01/1.02, delivery under 4.01) follow the two-Album pattern is left to be worked out against 2.02.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The requirement that the first Album of the first Option Period be \"comprised entirely\" of live Soviet-tour Master Recordings is followed by struck-through and hand-interlineated matter (apparently permitting additional non-live recordings), so the Album's permitted content cannot be read off the page. Whether \"entirely\" survives the alteration, and what the interlineation added, is precisely what a court would have to construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.52}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The label \"Live Album\" is fastened to the first Album of the first Option Period as described in the preceding, altered sentence of 3.06(b), so its content requirement is borrowed from a provision whose text is in doubt. Read with 4.01(a)(ii), which uses the same equation, the defined term may attach to an Album that is not in fact entirely live.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The single sentence gathers the Initial Period, the second and third Option Periods and the fourth Option Period and then fixes delivery at 120 days after \"commencement of such Period,\" leaving the antecedent of \"such Period\" to be supplied for each listed Album. The Initial Period limb is also spent, since that Period ran from 1985 and this amendment is dated April 3, 1989.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The fixed May 29, 1989 date is stated without reference to when the first Option Period commences, yet under paragraph 1.02 of the Agreement PRI may exercise the option at any time before expiration of the current Period and under amended 6.01(b)(i) a quarter of the Advance falls due on commencement. The delivery date can therefore precede, or long follow, the events the payment and term provisions tie it to.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The limb governing the second Album of the Initial Period measures delivery from delivery of that Period's first Album, but the Initial Period began in 1985 and had run before this April 1989 amendment, so the window it creates is retrospective. Read with amended 4.01(a)(i), which likewise still fixes an Initial Period deadline, it is unclear whether these Initial Period limbs have any operation at all.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Disapplying the whole of paragraph 4.01(d) to the Live Album removes not only the sixty-day grace period in 4.01(d)(i) but also 4.01(d)(ii)'s suspension of the delivery date when the parties cannot agree on the co-producer under paragraph 3.02(i). Whether the parties meant to strip that co-producer protection as well is left open by the blanket cross-reference.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"The applicable amount set forth below\" points to a table numbering Albums First through Ninth without tying any Album number to a Contract Period or to the Minimum Recording Obligation, so which figure is \"applicable\" to a given Album must be inferred. The problem is sharpened because this replacement table (nine Albums, differing amounts) supersedes the Agreement's eight-Album table.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The trigger \"within sixty (60) days ... following the day of PRI's receipt of this agreement, fully executed by Grantor and Artist\" was carried verbatim from the 1985 Agreement into this 1989 amendment, so \"this agreement\" may mean either instrument. On either reading the Initial Period trigger is already spent, leaving the timing of that quarter of the Advance uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Making Grantor responsible for \"all Recording Costs or other costs in connection with making Master Recordings\" sits awkwardly with amended 6.01(b)(i) and with paragraph 3.02 of the Agreement, which deems approved a budget equal to the applicable Advance and has PRI schedule and book studio time. Whether the Advance is the recording fund out of which those costs are met, or a payment separate from them, is only answerable by reading the two together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The right to deduct \"from any and all monies payable hereunder, except mechanical royalty payments\" leaves \"hereunder\" and \"monies payable\" unbounded — it is not said whether they reach royalties cross-collateralized from the Polydor Agreements under paragraph 6.04 or amounts other than royalties. The single express carve-out for mechanical royalties invites an expressio unius reading that everything else is fair game.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]}
]}

